# Diagnosis (checks/evidence/2026-10-25-T-049, scratch debugging of one
# SimPy replication): the script's own bug, not the kernel's. C-S1's
# calendar starts off shift (S(0) = 0 until 360) and the script asked for
# blockers only at a change of S, never for S(0): its machine served the
# jobs that arrived before the first shift (overtime in [W, 360) and less
# backlog later). The kernel's numbers agree with a back-of-the-envelope
# count (day 0: about 330 jobs x 3 min = 990 unit-minutes; day 1 fully busy
# on [2280, 2760): 960; in use about 1956 vs Go's 1960). The fix blocks the
# units off shift at t=0 before anything runs, without recording a change
# (S(0) is the program's value, D-047). After it every comparison passes,
# 140 of 140 (simulation-reference-test.log). G-C2 (S(0) = 0) was not
# affected: its first arrival is at the first shift start.
